# Skill: feature-bug-analyst

Read and follow `skills/feature-builder/feature-bug-analyst/SKILL.md`. Fill `skills/feature-builder/feature-bug-analyst/assets/what-to-build.md` only.

Announce: `Using skill: feature-bug-analyst`.

## Job

Turn a reported defect into a locked fix specification. Ask only landmines that still matter. Locate evidence in the repo. Deliver `agent-engineer-skills/<name>/what-to-build.md` so `feature-developer` can write the failing test first, then a minimal fix.

## Must

1. Restate Expected vs Actual. Add nothing. Name the kind of work from the request and the repo.
2. If the request is missing-feature product work, stop and name `feature-specifier`.
3. If path (or symbol), Expected, and Actual are already present, skip the question batch. Otherwise ask only remaining landmines (expected/actual, reproduction, environment when symptom-specific, state/data, impact) in one `AskQuestion` batch. Do not only print A/B/C in the chat.
4. Search the tree. Rank two or three hypotheses. Confirm or reject with `path:line` or equivalent facts. May run existing tests for evidence. Do not add tests or edit source.
5. Write every section of the bug `what-to-build.md` template, including proposed failing test, minimal fix approach, and regression risks.
6. Before handing over, check the file against `Before you finish` in `SKILL.md`. Fix what fails.

## Must not

- Write product code or edit/add tests on disk
- Invent a precise root cause without evidence
- Invent edge cases, algorithms, or hardening outside Reproduction and Done when
- Prescribe a defensive rewrite or call-graph tour beyond the fix paths
- Write `prd.md`, `clarification-log.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `concept.md`, or `notes.md`
- Leave "handle it appropriately" for the developer
- Write instructions about how to fill the file into the file itself
- Log secrets

## Do not use

When the idea is a new capability without an existing contract (`feature-specifier`), a greenfield/MVP design (`mvp-specifier`), a messy-module restructure with no defect (`feature-refactorer`), or the user only wants code, review, or tests on an existing specification.
